  "modified": "2026-11-02T11:03:38Z",
  "details": "The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: ipv6: exthdrs: refresh nh pointer after ipv6_hop_jumbo() (CVE-2026-63924)\n  * kernel: ipv6: exthdrs: refresh nh after handling HAO option (CVE-2026-63922)\n  * kernel: af_unix: Fix UAF read of tail->len in unix_stream_data_wait() (CVE-2026-64109)\n  * kernel: scsi: target: core: Fix iSCSI ISID use-after-free in REGISTER AND MOVE (CVE-2026-72083)\n  * kernel: tipc: require net admin for TIPCv2 netlink mutators (CVE-2026-74283)\n  * kernel: smb: client: bound dirent name against end of SMB response in cifs_filldir (CVE-2026-93787)\n  * kernel: ZDI-CAN-33367: Linux Kernel skbuff skb_zerocopy Improper Ownership Management Local Privilege Escalation Vulnerability ()\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
